      "body": "## Motivation\n\n`validate_deepseek_v41_features` only accepts Mooncake and NIXL (#43734) for DeepSeek-V4.1 DSpark PD, so `--disaggregation-transfer-backend mori` fails at startup. The V4.1 DSpark PD support is backend-agnostic: the layout and TP checks run in `CommonKVManager.try_ensure_parallel_info`, and MoRI already transfers the target and draft SWA states through its generic state path.\n\n## Modifications\n\nAccept `mori` next to `mooncake` and `nixl` in the V4.1 DSpark PD check and update the error message.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nDeepSeek-V4.1-Flash, 1P1D on one 8x MI355X node (prefill TP4 + decode TP4), DSpark, MoRI, `lmsysorg/sglang-rocm:v0.5.21-rocm724-mi35x-20261003` + this PR:\n\n| Test | 1P1D MoRI | Aggregated (reference) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Needle at 213 / 1.1K / 2.7K / 5.4K / 21K / 110K prompt tokens | all correct | all correct |\n| GSM8K 5-shot, 400 questions | 0.907 | 0.900 - 0.910 |\n| DSpark accept length (decode) | 3.46 | 3.4 - 3.5 |\n| Chat with thinking, tool call | correct | correct |\n\nWith the UMBP direct linker on the prefill side (#42197), a 110K-token prompt after `flush_cache` on both servers restores 110,080 cached tokens and produces greedy output identical to the cold run.\n\nThese runs use CP=1 on both servers. Since #40323 the same check also admits prefill CP; MoRI with prefill CP is not covered here.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A: this only widens a startup check; the transfer path is unchanged.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38333740714](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38333740714)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38333740578](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38333740578)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38333740698](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38333740698)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
